WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.465
When you hire someone to build your home,

00:00:03.465 --> 00:00:06.225
three questions sit under every conversation.

00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:07.450
What will this cost?

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.300
What’s actually happening on site?

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.762
And where is my money going?

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:16.274
Infinity Lifespaces is a design-and-build firm in Gurugram.

00:00:16.325 --> 00:00:18.600
They answered those questions well in person.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.416
Their website and their tools didn’t answer them at all.

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:26.554
Keerthi was the UX designer for both the website and a client app.

00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:31.291
He took them from stakeholder conversations to final designs in eight weeks.

00:00:31.341 --> 00:00:34.182
Then he worked with the build team on implementation.

00:00:35.432 --> 00:00:41.120
Research on both sides of the table kept landing on the same three questions.

00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:45.520
Before signing, price was the last thing a visitor could find out on their own.

00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:49.469
During the build, clients couldn’t see progress without asking.

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:53.476
And payments were tracked by the firm, not shown to the person paying.

00:00:54.726 --> 00:00:58.610
So every major feature is an answer to one of those questions.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.510
Price first.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.725
A quotation calculator on the website gives an estimate in a few steps,

00:01:04.725 --> 00:01:08.225
putting the most anxious question at the top of the funnel,

00:01:08.225 --> 00:01:10.064
instead of behind a sales call.

00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:15.820
The site itself became cleaner and easier to scan, with one clear call to action,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:19.454
and a moodboard where clients collect their own inspiration.

00:01:20.304 --> 00:01:23.717
In the client app: show the site, not a status.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:27.170
Live video from the build replaces “it’s on track”,

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.372
and the team is one message away.

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:31.347
Money you can follow.

00:01:31.397 --> 00:01:34.569
Payments are laid out as milestones tied to the work,

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.442
with documents and materials right next to them.

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:42.150
And the calculator and the moodboard live inside the app too,

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.944
so a website visitor becomes a client without starting over.

00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:51.113
Looking back, Keerthi would measure the calculator from day one:

00:01:51.113 --> 00:01:53.257
how many estimates turn into calls.

00:01:53.306 --> 00:01:56.951
And he’d design the site team’s side of the app with the same care,

00:01:56.951 --> 00:02:01.086
because live updates only work if someone on site can post them in a minute.

00:02:01.936 --> 00:02:03.924
Design by Keerthi Vardhan.

